#!/usr/bin/python3
# Generated by Ask CK PyTest Creator for AWPTCM-T33235 — (3) Port - Fixed port Speed
# Standardized ART framework script. Frame is fixed; test logic is filled per step.
#
# ==== OBJECTIVE — expected results this script must demonstrate ====
#   - Each speed supported by the port configurable as an explicit fixed value, with the
#   operational speed matching the configured value.
#   - Auto-negotiation reported as disabled on a port carrying an explicit fixed speed,
#   distinguishing a forced speed from a negotiated one in the port's reported state.
#   - A link re-established at the newly configured speed after each speed change, without a
#   device restart.
#   - The port returned to its default negotiated behaviour when the fixed speed is removed
#   or set back to auto.
#   - A speed value that is invalid, out of range, or unsupported on the port's media type
#   rejected with a clear error, the previous valid configuration remaining in effect.
#   - No link established, and no spurious link-up reported, while the link partner is fixed
#   at an incompatible speed — the link returning once the partner is set to a compatible
#   value.
#   - The configured fixed speed retained across an administrative shutdown/no-shutdown
#   cycle and reapplied from saved configuration after a device restart.
#   - Fixed speed applied per port, with configuration of one port leaving the speed and
#   link state of other ports unchanged.
#   - Configured speed and operational speed reported consistently in port status and
#   configuration output.
# ==================================================================

